The utility checks the standard binary directories for the speci‐
fied  programs,  printing out the paths of any it finds.  The de‐
fault path searched is the string returned by the utility for the
string.  If the option is specified, then the value of the  envi‐
ronment  variable  is  used instead.  The utility exits 0 on suc‐
cess, 1 on general error, 2 if only some  programs  were  located
and  3  if  none  were.  The historic flags and arguments for the
utility are no longer available in this version.  The command ap‐
